As far as I understand it, the way tags work is, they take a sumti and then
say that the main selbri happens in relation to that sumti.

i.e. {mi citka ba lo nu mi xagji} is saying "I eat in the future of the
event that I am hungry".  Now if no sumti is provided then it's just {mi
citka ba zo'e} and I guess context assume that this means that {mi citka}
happens in the future of this speech act (i.e. it's future tense).

So really you can put {ca zo'e} or {ca ku} anywhere in the selbri to say
"this selbri happens 'ca' to zo'e".

